Z||000003||stimpy||05-08-2001||09:29 AM||||Get messy drunk at home.  It's cheaper and safer. Get it out of your system quick, because drinking may be cool and rebellious when you're uderage, once you turn 21 you're just a drunk.  By the time you hit 30 if you're still messin with it, you're an alcholoic. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously, the best part about turning 21 for me was the live band clubs I could now get into.  Go down to the record store and ask the guy with the weird piercings where to find the good shows at. Go rock out.<P>BTW, Happy @&%ing Birthday!!!!!!!!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||05-08-2001||09:38 AM||||well if you dont have anyone to go out drinking with, remember that the reason you feel intoxicated and your reactions slow down, and your speech gets slurred, and you feel like crap for a day or too after drinking alcohol is because:<P>  alcohol is poisionous!<P>When you get drunk you are partially (hopefully) poisioning yourself.<P>If you have nobody to go out drinking with, you could ingest a small amount of cyanide, lead, clorox, gasoline, salmonilla, or bug spray, and you would feel pretty much the same. Trick is figuring out the right amount to you get the desired near-death feeling without acutally killing yourself. (Lead is pretty cool cause it will cause you to walk around in a stupor for the rest of your life, instead of only for one day!)<P>Or you could celebrate the milestone of entering adult-hood by doing something else: Spend some quiet time alone and set a goal for yourself for the next year, five years, 20 years.<P>Go out and shop around for something you would want to work towards purchasing, a new car, a boat or jet ski, some new personal sporting equipment (downhill skis, racing bicycle, windsurfer or catamaran) take a skidiving lesson, take a flying lesson, learn to scuba dive.<P>  Take up something that you have always wanted to do but always put off: drawing, painting, rockclimbing, running, photography, buy an electric guitar, keyboard, set of drums...<P>  Take another look at your career descision, take a stab at deciding what you want to accomplish with your life, now that it is really just beginning.<P>   It totally amazes me how people from China or Vietnam come to the US and take advantage of the opportunities that exist here, and live each day with a passion, while people that grew up in America tend to squander the wealth of experiences and resources that are available to them.<P>  Do something positive to celebrate your 21st birthday. Do something you will look back on 50 years from now and say, that was a milestone in my life, that was a turning point.||||reg||1
