Z||000034||ferg||05-08-2001||08:15 PM||||Here are some places to go - <P>Bin Willy's- in valparaiso- club- (meat market)- always lots of cops, they hang out waiting to get drunks- sleazy looking women. Most guys look like they are on steroids, possible fighting on a regular basis.<P>Goodfella's - in valpo- mid 30's divorcee bar- older crowd.<P>Northside tap- again valpo - VU students/locals- for me it's a high school reunion- good drink specials- <P>Passtimes- valpo bar- laid back- cool place to go w/ friends- usually quieter place- not a hook-up bar- decent food- outdoor dining.<P>The court- good bar, old courthouse for valpo- the original jail cell is in there. I think they have live music.<P>Simentos- looks like a dump- but not bad inside, really big place- again valpo<P>Jackson's bar- Never been there- never goin either.<P>Inmans- bowling alley- karoke bar (bar is called 'empty pockets') but you can take beer out to the lanes. bowling alley- what more can I say<P>Aberdeen Brewing company- In aberdeen- micro-brew place. Kinda expensive. New place in nice neighborhood.<P>In chesterton- fin McCools (sp???) I got really really wasted there on St. patty's day. one year- good times- don't remember how to get there, only been once.<P>Used to be a place near you called the factory- don't remember if it's still up and running or not- never been there.<P>You can also go to chicago- take the south shore up there- lots and lots of bars up there- be prepared to spend BIG dollars- plan where you are going- take plenty of money<P>I stay away from places in Portage, Hobart, Gary, East Chicago, Merrillville, Michigan City. These places get rough and roudy at night. <P>You can always go to the boats- in Michigan city, Gary, East Chicago, hammond, etc- you can go there yourself, buy beers cheap- gamble. have a good time by yourself. <P>If you want a drive- go to New Buffalo, MI- place called Redamaks- great burgers- family place- good drinks- close (maybe- 30 minutes from you- ) next to lake michigan- they are located on US 12- if you went to michigan city indiana, made your way to US 12- then just drove into michigan (the state) you'll go right past this place, you'll also drive right past the Michigan City gambling boat (blue chip casino)<P>I've been to all the bars in Valpo that I mentioned- I usually don't go out that much anymore- but they haven't changed much. Just a warning- Bin willy's, goodfella's, and northside are on Calumet (old 49)- cops hang out there at night- consider yourself warned. the court and pass times are downtown- next to county and city cop shops.<P>taxi service ends pretty early I think- I'm not sure though- you'll have to check that. I've never taken taxi service myself.<P>If I was you- (in your situation) I'd go to the boats- take about $110- $100 to gamble- $10 to drink on- beers are $1.00 once you are on the boat- just have fun doing that. No one will notice that you are flying solo- hell- they'll barely take their eyes off the slots to look at you. <P>If you aren't into that/or want to go somewhere w/ your family- go to redamak's- good food- serve beer's and drinks- state ID won't cut it- need drivers license to drink up there. look up the number on the internet for specifics<P>BTW- happy b-day<P>||||reg||1
